","measurement_id":"MCTM-036086","value":"11.7 ± 0.8","numeric":11.7}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-036087","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"II","Cell_line":"CHO-K1","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"4.5 ± 0.8","IC50_Dark_value":4.5,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/chem.201805626","Year":2019,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-036087","value":"25 ± 4","numeric":25}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-036088","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"II","Cell_line":"MMC-2","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"0.30 ± 0.05","IC50_Dark_value":0.3,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/chem.201805626","Year":2019,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-036088","value":"2.70 ± 0.07","numeric":2.7}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-036089","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"II","Cell_line":"MDA-MB-231","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"0.94 ± 0.05","IC50_Dark_value":0.94,"Method":"Crystal violet","DOI":"10.1002/chem.201805626","Year":2019,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-036089","value":"25 ± 2","numeric":25}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-036090","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"II","Cell_line":"MCF-7","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"1.01 ± 0.09","IC50_Dark_value":1.01,"Method":"Crystal violet","DOI":"10.1002/chem.201805626","Year":2019,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-036090","value":"13.6 ± 0.9","numeric":13.6}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-038278","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"1b","Cell_line":"A2780","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"1.8 ± 0.2","IC50_Dark_value":1.8,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/acs.inorgchem.0c01541","Year":2020,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-038278","value":"1.9 ± 0.1","numeric":1.9}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-038279","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"1b","Cell_line":"A2780cisR","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"1.0 ± 0.1","IC50_Dark_value":1,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/acs.inorgchem.0c01541","Year":2020,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-038279","value":"6.2 ± 0.6","numeric":6.2}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"1b","value":0.63,"value_relation":"=","std":0.03,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","pH":7.4,"temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1021/acs.inorgchem.0c01541","year":2020,"record_id":"MLDB-001624","detection":"ICP-OES","method_description":"The shake-flask method was utilized to measure the log Po/w values of the platinum complexes. Octanol and PBS used in this experiment were presaturated by incubation with shaking of the biphasic mixtures at room temperature overnight. 0.3 mL aliquots of PBS solution containing 50 μM Pt(IV) complex (cisplatin, carboplatin, oxaliplatin, 1a–d, 2a–d, 2a′–d′, 3a–d, and 3a′–d′) were incubated with the presaturated octanol (0.3 mL) in 2.0 mL tubes. To obtain homogeneous solutions, a 5 min vortex treatment was indispensable. After that, the two-phase mixtures were kept shaking at room temperature for 1 h to establish the partition equilibrium and then separated by centrifugation. After digestion, the platinum content in each phase was determined by ICP-OES. Each sample was tested in triplicate. The log Po/w values were expressed as the average of the results."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"II","value":0.33,"value_relation":"=","std":0.08,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"200 mM NaCl","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1002/chem.201805626","year":2019,"record_id":"MLDB-002153","detection":"FAAS","method_description":"The partition coefficients (P) of the investigated platinum complexes were determined by the “shake flask” method. The complexes were dissolved in octanol-saturated water (OSW) containing 200 mm NaCl and mixed with water-saturated octanol (WSO) in volumetric ratios of 2:1, 1:1, and 1:2. Mixing was done by vortexing for 30 min at room temperature to establish the partition equilibrium. To separate the phases, centrifugation was done at 3000 g for 5 min. The layers were separated carefully by using a fine-tip pipette and then analyzed for metal content by flameless atomic absorption spectroscopy (FAAS). The partition coefficients were calculated as the ratio of the concentration of the compound in the octanol layer to that in the aqueous layer, log P=log ([Pt]WSO/[Pt]OSW)."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Pt(IV)AcOA","value":0.59,"value_relation":"=","std":0.04,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"200 mM NaCl","doi":"10.1038/s41598-017-03864-w","year":2017,"record_id":"MLDB-002192","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"To determine the partition coefficient (P) the shake flask method was used. Octanol-saturated water (OSW) and water-saturated octanol (WSO) were prepared using analytical grade octanol and 0.2 M aqueous NaCl solution (to suppress hydrolysis of the chlorido complexes). Compounds were first dissolved in DMF (compounds Pt(IV)diOA, Pt(IV)AcOA) or water (Pt(IV)diAc and cisplatin). Mixing was done by vortexing for 30 min at room temperature to establish the partition equilibrium. To separate the phases, centrifugation was done at 3000 g for 5 min. The aqueous layer was carefully separated from the octanol layer for platinum analysis. Platinum was quantified from aliquots taken from the octanol-saturated aqueous samples before and after partition by ICP-MS. Partition coefficients of Pt complexes were calculated using the equation log P = log ([Pt]WSO/[Pt]OSW)."}]}